 "intro": "Near Placentia (Piacenza) in northern Italy, early 271 AD. The Juthungi and Alamanni have got past Aurelian into Italy. You are the Emperor Aurelian, hurrying after them.",
 "debrief": "In the Historia Augusta and other late sources, the invaders ambushed Aurelian from woods near Placentia at dusk, and his army was badly beaten. Rome panicked, and the Sibylline Books were consulted. Aurelian regrouped and beat them at Fano and Pavia. Soon after, he began the Aurelian Walls around Rome, which still stand. The sources are brief and not fully reliable. The other choices are what-ifs.",
